.TH "SVGANIMATEDENUMERATION" "3JS" "July 9, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGAnimatedEnumeration \- SVGAnimatedEnumeration
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[B]\f[R] interface describes
attribute values which are constants from a particular enumeration and
which can be animated.
.PP
From SVG 2, both \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] and \f[CR]animVal\f[R] reflect the
non\-animated value of the attribute.
The allowed values of its properties depend on the associated attribute.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]baseVal\f[R]
An integer that is the base value of the given attribute before applying
any animations.
.TP
\f[B]animVal\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
This is the same as \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] in SVG 2.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
The \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] interface does not provide any
specific methods.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SH BASIC USAGE
Consider this snippet with a \f[CR]<clipPath>\f[R] element: Its
\f[CR]clipPathUnits\f[R] is associated with a
\f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] object.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 100 100\(dq width=\(dq200\(dq height=\(dq200\(dq>
  <\f[B]clipPath\f[R] id=\(dqclip1\(dq clipPathUnits=\(dquserSpaceOnUse\(dq>
    <\f[B]circle\f[R] cx=\(dq50\(dq cy=\(dq50\(dq r=\(dq35\(dq />
  </\f[B]clipPath\f[R]>

  \f[I]<!\-\- Some reference rect to materialized to clip path \-\->\f[R]
  <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqr1\(dq x=\(dq0\(dq y=\(dq0\(dq width=\(dq45\(dq height=\(dq45\(dq />
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
The following JavaScript gets the element, and logs the
\f[CR]baseVal\f[R] and \f[CR]animVal\f[R] of the
\f[CR]SVGClipPathElement.clipPathUnits\f[R] property.
These values should be the same.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] clipPathElt = document.getElementById(\(dqclip1\(dq);
console.log(clipPathElt.clipPathUnits.baseVal); \f[I]// Logs 1 that correspond to userSpaceOnUse\f[R]
console.log(clipPathElt.clipPathUnits.animVal); \f[I]// Logs 1 that correspond to userSpaceOnUse\f[R]
.EE
